{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines","id":1401716,"title":"[V5] Amalgams and Advanced Disciplines","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-08T11:05:01-07:00","id":1401716,"title":"[V5] Amalgams and Advanced Disciplines","content":"A place to discuss what sort of substitution can be made for +6 Disciplines, the role of Methuselah powers, and other story related mechanics.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T11:27:42-07:00","id":1401722,"title":"","content":"What substitution can be realistically done? The 6+ discipline up to ten made sense before, but for whatever reason it was fudged completely. Maybe when your PC gets &quot;older&quot; you can get access to more better &quot;powers/abilities&quot; to replace your already full discipline dots with? Maybe an &quot;evolution&quot; system of some sort? Regardless removing 6+ Disciplines was a really bad botch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:05:22-07:00","id":1401727,"title":"","content":"6+ was a bad system,<br /> the 6+ disciplines were too expensive for questionable usefulness/power/versatility,<br /> plus it didn't make sense for there to only be 5 or 6 disciplines at lvl 1-5, while 6+ had a alot of them, even if some of them would fit better in the 1-5 category<br /> <br /> I was thinking that rather than adding 6+ disciplines, the 1-5 disciplines would gain in potency as you lowered your generation becoming elder disciplines,<br /> <br /> for example,<br /> if you're high generation, dominate 2 requires eye contact,<br /> if you lower your generation to 7, your dominate 2 grows in potency and eye contact is no longer necessary, your voice or skin contact is enough (the equivalent of the dominate 6 power 'Command Obedience')<br /> <br /> you could also add the ability for high gens to use elders disciplines, but at a higher difficulty or higher blood cost (requiring more time or more blood expenditure, a bit like how it is for mages with arete 1)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-08-2020, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:06:10-07:00","id":1401728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401722#post1401722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What substitution can be realistically done? The 6+ discipline up to ten made sense before, but for whatever reason it was fudged completely. Maybe when your PC gets &quot;older&quot; you can get access to more better &quot;powers/abilities&quot; to replace your already full discipline dots with? Maybe an &quot;evolution&quot; system of some sort? Regardless removing 6+ Disciplines was a really bad botch.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's ways they could go around it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Advanced Disicplines&quot; are a cool house rule I've seen used and use myself. You'd make the Elder versions of Dominate, Presence, and so on with a requirement for the first 5 levels.<br /> <br /> That way the system doesn't break.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:06:43-07:00","id":1401729,"title":"","content":"Previous six+ powers will either be made into 4/5 level dot powers either directly or as high level amalgams. We've seen an example of this through Ancestral Dominion and Shatter in cults of the blood gods. Based on the Montano loresheet, Methuselah's and the like may be able to learn extra powers above the five that are allowed but the system doesn't really need special exclusive powers for them when amalgams serve that purpose plenty well. &quot;Why can the elder Ventrue dominate an entire family line and I can't? Because he has amalgams that I don't.&quot; In this case that one might be an auspex + dominate amalgam and a high level one at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:09:43-07:00","id":1401730,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, the purpose of 6+ disciplines in earlier editions was to make Elders scarier, and the main problem with them was that they spent precious wordcount on things most players would never have the chance to use. How often do you play fourth-gen characters with access to nine-dot powers, after all? They were good inspiration for STs, but there's a reason Gehenna replaced all dot-ten powers with &quot;Plot Device&quot;: if Arikel (or Helena for that matter) wants to make something happen with Presence, it generally happens, whether or not there's a printed power to do exactly that.<br /> <br /> V5's approach is instead to make Elders better at using their disciplines in general (Blood Potency buffs) in a way that takes less wordcount. That way every power printed can actually be relevant to players, while Elders still have the edge\u2014pools get bigger, flat bonuses get more potent, and powers get less costly to use (in terms of blood). Meanwhile, the cooler six- and seven-dot powers have gotten moved down into the 1-5 range.<br /> <br /> So for the big huge plot-device ancients, I would run them the way I've always run them: Ur-Shulgi can break the Tremere blood curse without having a nine-dot Break Tremere Blood Curse power, just because they're a terrifyingly powerful fourth-gen blood-sorcerer and their powers are plot devices more than anything else. For the smaller ancients, like Villon and Hardestadt, I let them buy additional powers from the 1-5 levels if applicable. They still only have five dots of Presence or Fortitude or whatever (because their potent blood adds to Discipline dice pools already and a second bonus just gets ridiculous), but they can have whatever specialized amalgams they need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:51:04-07:00","id":1401738,"title":"","content":"I think VtR took the right approach here:<br /> <br /> Disciplines are from 1-5.<br /> Devotions (aka Combo Disciplines, aka Amalgams) can include 1-3 Disciplines and don't mess with your core Discipline selection.<br /> Merits can adjust Disciplines, including having Blood Potency requirements.<br /> <br /> Nothing is out of reach of PCs (even if some is going to take a lot of XP to get), nothing besides Blood Potency goes over 5, lots of room to add custom powers to make characters (PCs and NPCs) a bit more unique, and the potential to give thousand of years old vampires some really scary powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T12:57:47-07:00","id":1401739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401728#post1401728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's ways they could go around it.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Advanced Disicplines&amp;quot; are a cool house rule I've seen used and use myself. You'd make the Elder versions of Dominate, Presence, and so on with a requirement for the first 5 levels.<br /> <br /> That way the system doesn't break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too late to that.. Helena &amp; CIA sheets were already printed without those advanced gimmik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:02:31-07:00","id":1401741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401739#post1401739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Too late to that.. Helena &amp; CIA sheets were already printed without those advanced gimmik.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they're suffering the Withering from resisting the Beckoning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:04:30-07:00","id":1401743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade\"> Vampire: The Masquerade - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A gothic-punk game of personal horror. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:17:12-07:00","id":1401746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401741#post1401741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe they're suffering the Withering from resisting the Beckoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>You changed your mind about this topic? <br /> <br /> In a previous post some months ago you replied to me that vampires that didn't resist beckoning don't need an explanation in the book for what they can and cannot do, that they can do anything they want and that players would not roll dice if they tried to kill such beings, in this caze they just needed to describe the plan and the ST would arbitrarily decide whether or not they could do it. you gave an example of the players using a truck full of something exploding to kill a Methuselah as a valid idea, in which there should be no dice roll, just the acceptance of st.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:58:18-07:00","id":1401755,"title":"","content":"I'll maintain the following:<br /> <br /> The original discipline system was secretly genius. It was simple, intuitive, disciplines mostly came in a rational order, and it worked with metaphysics and magical theory. The player and the character needed to put little thought into what disciplines to get, they were just extensions of a character. It also had a big impact on the social dynamics of the game; Exceeding level 5 disciplines gave incentive to diablerise. Individual powers might've been bad, but the system was near perfect...<br /> <br /> Combo disciplines, as written, weren't something I liked. Individual powers might've been great, but the system of combo disciplines needed work.<br /> <br /> And now we've moved on to amalgams. How have they improved on the much flawed combo discipline system? They haven't, they're amplications of what I dislike about V5's overchoice system: not only are you trying to work out which of the specific powers you'll get at each level of the discipline, you'll also have to plan to around other disciplines to get the powers you want &quot;So I got my Domainte to 3 and now I want to buy a 4th dot but I want this amalgam power so I'll have to wait on getting two more points of auspex before I improve dominate again...<br /> <br /> Like, what? I don't think this is a good feature. The more I think about it, the worse it gets. Surely 6+ powers, of which you can buy different things at the same level if you wanted to, was a better, simpler, less nitty-gritty system. I don't understand a push for more amalgams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T13:59:31-07:00","id":1401756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401746#post1401746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You changed your mind about this topic?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but it's a subject that clearly is bothering a lot of people. Even if I don't agree with it, I think it's important people have options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a previous post some months ago you replied to me that vampires that didn't resist beckoning don't need an explanation in the book for what they can and cannot do, that they can do anything they want and that players would not roll dice if they tried to kill such beings, in this caze they just needed to describe the plan and the ST would arbitrarily decide whether or not they could do it. you gave an example of the players using a truck full of something exploding to kill a Methuselah as a valid idea, in which there should be no dice roll, just the acceptance of st. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think that stating out beings like Helena and Mithras is a mistake. One of the smartest moves in gaming, I think, was when they did the LORD OF THE RINGS adaptation for Decipher and listed Sauron's stats as, &quot;You lose.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think that Methuselahs should be plot devices, basically.<br /> <br /> However, if you are going to do an Advanced System, you shouldn't feel beholden to the stats already published and say, &quot;Helena has no stats over 5 nor does Mithras when restored to full strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401755#post1401755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll maintain the following:<br /> <br /> The original discipline system was secretly genius.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wasn't.<br /> <br /> The powers listed were inconsistent, disorganized, and very much removed a lot of mystery from the Antediluvians. By statting them out, you made Methuselahs easy to kill and that removed a lot of the mystery from the game.<br /> <br /> I also felt that Elders had very inconsistent levels of power between the editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-08-2020, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:31:22-07:00","id":1401767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401755#post1401755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original discipline system was secretly genius. It was simple, intuitive, disciplines mostly came in a rational order, and it worked with metaphysics and magical theory. The player and the character needed to put little thought into what disciplines to get, they were just extensions of a character. It also had a big impact on the social dynamics of the game; Exceeding level 5 disciplines gave incentive to diablerise. Individual powers might've been bad, but the system was near perfect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but from what I've seen in other threads, your justification of the system is &quot;G#d/Lilith/the Antediluvians imposed these mechanics and therefore they're perfect because they're divine&quot;. You could just as well claim that G#d created the V5 disciplines and therefore they're infallible too.<br /> <br /> Why does it make sense that Lasombra can't see through shadows if they're higher than Gen 7? That should be a low-level, fundamental power, not something you need to be an Elder for. But it's stuck at level 6, because there was already a progression of powers for 1-5 and no room to add something new.<br /> <br /> Or, why is the first step of Quietus &quot;you make a magical sphere of silence&quot;, and the second step &quot;you turn your blood into poison&quot;? What's the connection between those?<br /> <br /> Why does Animalism swing sharply back and forth between controlling animals and controlling the Beast? Why do you always have to switch from one to the other and then back again as you develop your powers, for no obvious reason?<br /> <br /> Why do only four clans not have a special discipline all their own? What's different about those four clans?<br /> <br /> (All mechanics taken from V20, because that's the corebook I have on hand at the moment.) I don't hate the 1-5 discipline system, but I think claiming it's &quot;near perfect&quot; is a serious overstatement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:31:22-07:00","id":1401768,"title":"","content":"The system, not the specific powers within, was good. There are lots of little fine-tuning and I'll agree with you in that 8/9 powers could've been kept as myths and legends (The great madness of 1719 was theorized to be the work of a malkavian methuselah working with dementation of the ninth level... ) rather than something stated out like it was normal. But the 1-5 linear, 6+ whatever system itself was magnificent, both from a story and gameplay perspective, even if we'd all like to go over certain powers with a pen and certain disciplines (presence, looking at you) don't really have intuitive, logical progression of other disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:39:47-07:00","id":1401771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401768#post1401768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system, not the specific powers within, was good.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue with the system as a whole, then, is that it's too rigid. When there are multiple things you want to make available at a low level, you have to either group them all into a single power (Auspex 1 sharpens your senses AND breaks invisibility AND gives premonitions) or shove one of them up to level six or higher (Obten 1 was taken, so seeing in darkness has to be Obten 6 now). <i>Sense the Beast</i> (new in V5) is a good Animalism power, and helps reinforce that Animalism is both the discipline of beasts and the discipline of the Beast, but there's no room in the fixed 1-5 hierarchy for it, so it can't exist in V20.<br /> <br /> One solution is what Requiem 1e did: at some levels there's a choice of two powers and you can only take one or the other, not both. Another solution is what Requiem 2e did: there's one power per level, but some powers unlock devotions (combo disciplines) that require only that specific power and give an alternate power of similar potency. I'm not a huge fan of either of these techniques.<br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I'd keep the &quot;multiple options per level&quot; idea from V5, but get rid of the opportunity costs. Someone who takes Obten 1 (Shadow Play) can also take Obten 1 (See In Darkness) without losing out on anything else. Not all levels need tons of options, but there are a few places where they'd be really nice to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:43:17-07:00","id":1401772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One of the smartest moves in gaming, I think, was when they did the LORD OF THE RINGS adaptation for Decipher and listed Sauron's stats as, &quot;You lose.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I think this is very shallow tbh.<br /> <br /> Why would I buy a rpg book if I will have to made up things on my own anyway? In vtm is not a matter if the Meth win or lose but what he can and can not do. I do not like neither as st or player to asspull never mentioned before especific powers to make something happen &quot;for the plot&quot;. No dice rolled no system no explanation, just a sea of random powers. Something I liiked in VtM is that my character someday can get there, and have the all cool powers (at last is possible) all I have to do is live long enough (while in v5, no way with the 1xp per game rule) I liked when the same rules that apply to npcs apply to pcs as well, because even if the scenario of the game is ruthless, the mechanics of the game are fair. <br /> As a ST Iwould feel bad to made up some BS Meth powers as the game go. It would feel like I cheated against the players. Its like not rolling dice in D&amp;D and simple declaring round after round &quot;the dragon rolled 20 because I say so&quot;. Have separate rules to Pcs and Npcs make the Pcs feel special in the world, too, going against the theme &quot;you are only one among many, many of us&quot;. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401756#post1401756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> However, if you are going to do an Advanced System,</div> </div> </div> </div>They will not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:50:08-07:00","id":1401775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401772#post1401772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I liiked in VtM is that my character someday can get there, and have the all cool powers (at last is possible) all I have to do is live long enough (while in v5, no way with the 1xp per game rule) I liked when the same rules that apply to npcs apply to pcs as well, because even if the scenario of the game is ruthless, the mechanics of the game are fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>But one of the core conceits of VtM's setting (as opposed to VtR's) is that you <i>can't</i> ever catch up to the Elders. Unless you're willing to consume people's souls, there's a glass ceiling you'll never be able to break through. That's been the case since the beginning, and is the whole point of Generation as a mechanic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:55:35-07:00","id":1401777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401767#post1401767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, but from what I've seen in other threads, your justification of the system is &quot;G#d/Lilith/the Antediluvians imposed these mechanics and therefore they're perfect because they're divine&quot;. You could just as well claim that G#d created the V5 disciplines and therefore they're infallible too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woah, I might have said something like that, but you're taking the wrong thing from it. <br /> <br /> If we appy gnostic thought, we can say that vampires are an emanation: A &quot;divine&quot; thing has fallen into our reality, starting off as divine and not limited to our reality's rules, but becoming less and less divine and more material as it descends. This can be seen in how the Generations become weaker after each embrace, each less capable of trancendant power than the last; IE their ability cap continues to lower till it's five, and as humans are limited to &quot;5 dots&quot; in attributes and abilities by the reality they're in, so too does it seem that reality props up disciplines to level 5 in a certain way. But the thing about Emanations in Gnostic thought is that once the fallen thing has reached the bottom, it'll fly hard back up. <br /> If we apply hermetic thought, vampirism is essentially alchemy. <br /> <br /> The important Caveat of these ideas is that we're not learning new things through this alchemy or Emanation; we're not learning up to five weirdly-specific powers through drinking blood; we're unlocking our potential. We are divine souls locked in a material world and we're trying to break out. I think it's all very romantic. The original system reflected that heavily, the new system and &quot;do I choose to jump high or do I choose to punch harder&quot;. unfortunately does not, my perspective says it feels very gamey, and amalgams feel very inconvenient. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:56:02-07:00","id":1401778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why does Animalism swing sharply back and forth between controlling animals and controlling the Beast? Why do you always have to switch from one to the other and then back again as you develop your powers, for no obvious reason?<br /> </div> </div> </div>With this I disagree. Animalism allow you excel control over the beast, period.<br /> Using you own beast to communicate with the beast within the animal is how you can talk, give orders etc etc with them. <br /> In v5, Idk what animalism is about? I did not read the lore beyond it just read the levels. The first power you have a pet and thats all but idk if the same results cannot be obtained be simply ghouling a dog.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:59:06-07:00","id":1401779,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with your conclusion about the role of Methuselahs in V:tM: that they should be basically be used as plot devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T14:59:41-07:00","id":1401780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401775#post1401775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But one of the core conceits of VtM's setting (as opposed to VtR's) is that you <i>can't</i> ever catch up to the Elders. Unless you're willing to consume people's souls, there's a glass ceiling you'll never be able to break through. That's been the case since the beginning, and is the whole point of Generation as a mechanic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In VtM you can. Just have to eat someone or start in dark ages and get a 6 dot at chargen. Follow the path of blood and be happy.<br /> In VtR your character, someday, will have torpor+amnesia and lose the blood potence anyway, while in vtm what you gain is your forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:09:55-07:00","id":1401782,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> I agree with you. Social mobility within the Camarilla in V:tM is much more restricted than it is in the various Covenants in V:tR because Generation acts as that glass ceiling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:29:32-07:00","id":1401786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401778#post1401778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With this I disagree. Animalism allow you excel control over the beast, period.<br /> Using you own beast to communicate with the beast within the animal is how you can talk, give orders etc etc with them.<br /> In v5, Idk what animalism is about? I did not read the lore beyond it just read the levels. The first power you have a pet and thats all but idk if the same results cannot be obtained be simply ghouling a dog.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is with how the powers don't seem to overlap between the two. Imagine a hypothetical redesigned Animalism where the first dot is &quot;communicate with animals <i>and frenzied vampires</i>&quot;, the third dot is &quot;snap someone out of frenzy <i>or shut down instincts</i>&quot;, etc. That would unify the two different themes of &quot;animals&quot; and &quot;the Beast&quot; much more to my liking.<br /> <br /> In V5, it's basically the same as it always was (you can talk to animals, summon animals, shut down frenzy, possess animals, put your frenzies into someone else), plus a few extra powers. <i>Sense the Beast</i> is a new level-one that lets you passively sense if someone has a Beast or not, and actively determine how hungry a vampire is. <i>Bond Famulus</i> is also level one and lets you buff an animal and make it so you can use all other Animalism powers on it at no cost. <i>Animal Succulence</i> lets you get more vitae from eating animals. Those are the main additions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T15:37:51-07:00","id":1401788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401786#post1401786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue is with how the powers don't seem to overlap between the two. Imagine a hypothetical redesigned Animalism where the first dot is &amp;quot;communicate with animals <i>and frenzied vampires</i>&amp;quot;, the third dot is &amp;quot;snap someone out of frenzy <i>or shut down instincts</i>&amp;quot;, etc. That would unify the two different themes of &amp;quot;animals&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;the Beast&amp;quot; much more to my liking.<br /> <br /> In V5, it's basically the same as it always was (you can talk to animals, summon animals, shut down frenzy, possess animals, put your frenzies into someone else), plus a few extra powers. <i>Sense the Beast</i> is a new level-one that lets you passively sense if someone has a Beast or not, and actively determine how hungry a vampire is. <i>Bond Famulus</i> is also level one and lets you buff an animal and make it so you can use all other Animalism powers on it at no cost. <i>Animal Succulence</i> lets you get more vitae from eating animals. Those are the main additions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Get it. Why v5 didn't fixed it? Missed oportunity.<br /> About the other level 1 power...<br /> Omg... Sense the Beast was only a Merit in VtM o.o A very especific power to be a discipline level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:38:04-07:00","id":1401803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401727#post1401727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">plus it didn't make sense for there to only be 5 or 6 disciplines at lvl 1-5, while 6+ had a alot of them, even if some of them would fit better in the 1-5 category)</div> </div> </div> </div>Every dot in a discipline pre-V5 discipline system packed numerous powers altogether at once with each progression you made into it. It didn't have the &quot;1 power per dot&quot; crap V5 has now, so saying that only the 6-10 disciplines only &quot;have alot&quot; makes no sense within itself, not the other way around.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But one of the core conceits of VtM's setting (as opposed to VtR's) is that you <i>can't</i> ever catch up to the Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you even talking about? Part of the 6+ discipline system by itself was an avenue to show that the abilities of the &quot;Elders&quot; are obtainable and the fact that you can become one yourself. I 100% agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24832_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24832\" data-vbnamecard=\"24832\">blailton</a>, what made pre-V5 good was that the NPCs weren't special at all or the PCs for that matter- you CAN get to the level of discipline mastery Elders have over a few decades or centuries (months if you train it good enough). It never or should be somesort of &quot;conceit&quot; at all that way- unless you want to RP as a Thinblood- but it certainly IS possible to catch up to the Elders. What you say isn't core at all... well that is until V5 completely wrecked the opportunity of PCs every roleplaying as an Elder or getting to their level of power with a pure hamfist of removing 6+ disciplines in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 07-08-2020, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:53:14-07:00","id":1401807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401803#post1401803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every dot in a discipline pre-V5 discipline system packed numerous powers altogether at once with each progression you made into it. It didn't have the &quot;1 power per dot&quot; crap V5 has now, so saying that only the 6-10 disciplines only &quot;have alot&quot; makes no sense within itself, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't mention V5 a single time, and I certainly wasn't defending it,<br /> I was only criticising the pre-v5 systems and giving my own thoughts on how 6+ disciplines could better be implemented (only on the surface level though, because I don't think I have what it takes to go in depth)<br /> <br /> if you want my opinion on the v5 system,<br /> I like some of it, don't like most of it...I would use a few of its ideas, but overall it's not for me,<br /> that doesn't mean the pre-v5 stuff doesn't need a rework","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 07-08-2020, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T19:57:09-07:00","id":1401833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401803#post1401803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Every dot in a discipline pre-V5 discipline system packed numerous powers altogether at once</b> with each progression you made into it. It didn't have the &quot;1 power per dot&quot; crap V5 has now, so saying that only the 6-10 disciplines only &quot;have alot&quot; makes no sense within itself, not the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like how a Lasombra from the Clan of Shadows needs to be seventh-gen or lower to see through supernatural darkness?<br /> <br /> Seriously, I can't see any reason why that wasn't a level-one power from the start, except that there could only be one level-one power and Shadow Play had taken that slot already. Thematically, the Lasombra should be the best at seeing through supernatural darkness, seeing how often they create and manipulate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T20:02:22-07:00","id":1401834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401803#post1401803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you even talking about? Part of the 6+ discipline system by itself was an avenue to show that the abilities of the &quot;Elders&quot; are obtainable and the fact that you can become one yourself. I 100% agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24832_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24832\" data-vbnamecard=\"24832\">blailton</a>, what made pre-V5 good was that the NPCs weren't special at all or the PCs for that matter- you CAN get to the level of discipline mastery Elders have over a few decades or centuries (months if you train it good enough). It never or should be somesort of &quot;conceit&quot; at all that way- unless you want to RP as a Thinblood- but it certainly IS possible to catch up to the Elders. What you say isn't core at all... well that is until V5 completely wrecked the opportunity of PCs every roleplaying as an Elder or getting to their level of power with a pure hamfist of removing 6+ disciplines in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your Generation puts a cap on your power level that's fixed at chargen, and raising it later requires breaking the ultimate taboo and eating people's souls. The thematic idea, presumably, was that the Elders weren't just stronger because they were old\u2014they were stronger because they started with advantages that you didn't, and have built systems to keep it that way. That's why Generation was so immutable (and why the one means of changing it was the worst possible sin in vampiric society).<br /> <br /> If the devs didn't want that theme, I imagine they would have done it Requiem-style, where Elders <i>don't</i> have any inherent advantage apart from being old (and having centuries' worth of xp on their sheets). In Requiem, there's no limit imposed on how strong you can get, it just takes time and experience.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying it's a bad theme or anything like that. Just, it's a theme that's been part of Masquerade from the start. And I highly doubt that most VtM players, in any edition, have ever had a nine-dot power on their character sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T20:50:09-07:00","id":1401842,"title":"","content":"Even with the present constraints, elders in V5 are plenty scary. They don\u2019t need <i>more </i>powers to be so, though the traditional method of branching out into additional disciplines still accomplishes that. In fact, it\u2019s more effective in the long run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T01:31:28-07:00","id":1401873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401833#post1401833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like how a Lasombra from the Clan of Shadows needs to be seventh-gen or lower to see through supernatural darkness?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know you can always see through your own darkness? In some versions (DAV20 i think) Auspex/Protean can also confound this power.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't see how V5 has improved on anything there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Players should just choose their disciplines based on simple wants and not have to worry about the finer details of what kind of powers they're getting. 'Potence is super strength, Dominate is the power of telling people what to do and then how to think, chimestry is making better and better illusions'<br /> It's easier for players<br /> It's makes a lot more narrative sense.<br /> <br /> Having players not only pick which fields of powers they have but also the very specific powers within these fields is both a bad mechanic due to overchoce (Do I pick this or this or this or this or this or...) and a bad story device in that each power is absurdly specific; Before, I could use the strength of potence to help me swim,climb, jump, lift, throw, grapple or deliver extra damage through a strike or anything otherwise considered strength... Now each power is very specific with one of those things and you've got to wonder why the vampire who can jump double his height can't push or lift or throw or strike any better than a regular dude. (Gifts, at least, make sense in that they're abilities granted by spirits to half-spirit warriors, and also they're not grouped together in a 1-5 strength themed order you have to work through)<br /> <br /> Amalgams are just an exaggeration of the mechanical problem; You need to plan not only what your 1-5 is but you also need to have a certain amount of another discipline to proceed. Just imagine your vampire saying &quot;I need to stop with the sanguine blood, because if I want that very specific next power I need to first increase that other discipline through Choleric blood&quot; (but at least I found blood that helps me jump!)<br /> <br /> Simplicity is better. Amalgams are a needless additional complication","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-09-2020, 04:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:21:05-07:00","id":1401896,"title":"","content":"the way i see it the V5 discipline system is supposed to give the player more options but still keep their power level limited. the issue being that how they limit their abilities. it's either a hard limit on your abilities or (like with amalgams) they have a cost associated with them that are just dull and uninteresting.<br /> <br /> so as an example of a 'fix' (i'm not a game designer this is just to get my point across): &quot;unliving hive&quot; is an animalism mainly used by the nos and to enforce this they made it an amalgam with obfuscate. i'd suggest that instead of an amalgam you had to take one dot in a &quot;deformed visage&quot; flaw for each hive you wanted to host, not only would nosferatu be more willing to pay said price then other animalism users due to the nos being ugly by nature. on top of that older nos are more hidious due to bane severity and thus would be less affected from taking additional points in said flaw but on top of that are also able to ghoul more swarms that they could host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T05:40:32-07:00","id":1401903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>archderd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401896#post1401896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the way i see it the V5 discipline system is supposed to give the player more options but still keep their power level limited. the issue being that how they limit their abilities. it's either a hard limit on your abilities or (like with amalgams) they have a cost associated with them that are just dull and uninteresting.<br /> <br /> so as an example of a 'fix' (i'm not a game designer this is just to get my point across): &quot;unliving hive&quot; is an animalism mainly used by the nos and to enforce this they made it an amalgam with obfuscate. i'd suggest that instead of an amalgam you had to take one dot in a &quot;deformed visage&quot; flaw for each hive you wanted to host, not only would nosferatu be more willing to pay said price then other animalism users due to the nos being ugly by nature. on top of that older nos are more hidious due to bane severity and thus would be less affected from taking additional points in said flaw but on top of that are also able to ghoul more swarms that they could host.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Have swarms inside body is a Baali thing btw not a Nos thing)<br /> <br /> I agree with you, but some cases would be tricky...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 07-09-2020, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T06:02:28-07:00","id":1401909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401903#post1401903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Have swarms inside body is a Baali thing btw not a Nos thing)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>you might wanna take a look at the description of 'unliving hive' in the V5 corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with you, but some cases would me tricky... </div> </div> </div>i don't expect every ability to have an interesting limitation, my point is more so that it *seems* the writers didn't even consider how to make the limitations of disciplines interesting and that it is an issue the current system is suffering from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T07:58:09-07:00","id":1401917,"title":"","content":"On paper, the V5 system gives more options, but in reality it gives the character less options. As said before, potence used to give you -all the strength- and you could do what you wanted with it, whilst nuPotence gives you a choice of very specific aplications, Auspex did a lot more at each level than what choices nuAuspex offers, and the same goes for most disciplines; V5 powers are extremely specific whilst the old disciplines were far more broadly applicable to a wider range of problems. NuDominate offers some things that Dominate doesn't have (at level 5 and below that is) but Dominate in practice was far, far more versatile; Command could do more, Mesmorize could do a lot more, forgetfull mind could do a lot more... and of course the things exclusive to nuDominate 1-5 could be done by Dominate 6+.<br /> <br /> You could say V5 gives you a lot of choice for keys on a keyring, but Disciplines used to give you an ever improving skeleton key (or a GEP gun).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T09:54:16-07:00","id":1401927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401917#post1401917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On paper, the V5 system gives more options, but in reality it gives the character less options. As said before, potence used to give you -all the strength- and you could do what you wanted with it, whilst nuPotence gives you a choice of very specific aplications, Auspex did a lot more at each level than what choices nuAuspex offers, and the same goes for most disciplines; V5 powers are extremely specific whilst the old disciplines were far more broadly applicable to a wider range of problems. NuDominate offers some things that Dominate doesn't have (at level 5 and below that is) but Dominate in practice was far, far more versatile; Command could do more, Mesmorize could do a lot more, forgetfull mind could do a lot more... and of course the things exclusive to nuDominate 1-5 could be done by Dominate 6+.<br /> <br /> You could say V5 gives you a lot of choice for keys on a keyring, but Disciplines used to give you an ever improving skeleton key (or a GEP gun).</div> </div> </div> </div>For the physical disciplines, the fairest comparison is probably to the MET versions, which have a new power at each level (in a 1-5 progression). Honestly I think Requiem handled these best, giving you both passive enhancements that scale with your dots and <i>also</i> active effects you can activate, which helps players feel like they're actually doing something; V20 physical disciplines imo suffered from being &quot;boring but practical&quot;, and vampire powers should never be boring.<br /> <br /> Auspex doing three different things at level one feels like a symptom of the problem I was talking about earlier. Auspex 1 is <i>really good</i> compared to the first level of other disciplines, letting you have enhanced senses AND pierce supernatural illusions AND get premonitions, which is why in my experience it's the most commonly taken out-of-clan. Now, I agree those things shouldn't be mutually exclusive (and that it's a weakness of V5 that they are)! But in my ideal system you'd have to pay for enhanced senses and supernatural premonitions separately. Take both if you want them both, otherwise take whichever fits more and move on to the higher dots.<br /> <br /> For Dominate, I still think your reading of V20 Mesmerize (that it lets you rewrite thoughts and beliefs as well as giving commands) is not what the book intended. For Command, in V5 you're no longer limited to a single word; the limitation is now on the duration of the action, which I like better. The main thing that's changed is you can't use Dominate for interrogation (either Mesmerize or Forgetful Mind), which is a nerf, but not as severe of one as it's usually depicted.<br /> <br /> (Thematically, I also believe old-style Conditioning is something you should still be able to do in V5, it just isn't a specific discipline power: it involves repeatedly using whatever Dominate power you like on someone over and over until their mind bends to your will, combined with a blood-bond if you want it, and that falls under the Project system. But this isn't spelled out in the book; hopefully the Player's Guide will talk more about it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T10:02:34-07:00","id":1401930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401873#post1401873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know you can always see through your own darkness? In some versions (DAV20 i think) Auspex/Protean can also confound this power.<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't see how V5 has improved on anything there.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Lasombra with the first level of Obten can now see through all darkness, supernaturally-inflicted or natural, including darkness produced by other Lasombra. I say it's an improvement, because it makes more thematic sense that when the Lasombra throws down a Stygian Shroud/Shroud of Night, the other Lasombra should be better equipped to see through it than the Gangrel.<br /> <br /> It's not a <i>huge</i> improvement, but one of my minor gripes with V20 Obtenebration was that it had ridiculously strong powers at low levels, while &quot;see in darkness&quot; was a level-six. Obten started as an antagonist-only power and later editions never quite figured out how to balance it for player use while keeping its concept intact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1401873#post1401873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Amalgams are just an exaggeration of the mechanical problem; You need to plan not only what your 1-5 is but you also need to have a certain amount of another discipline to proceed. Just imagine your vampire saying &quot;I need to stop with the sanguine blood, because if I want that very specific next power I need to first increase that other discipline through Choleric blood&quot; (but at least I found blood that helps me jump!)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem with Amalgams is the opportunity-cost mechanic: the way each Auspex power you take makes the next one harder instead of easier. In my ideal world, Amalgams would still exist, but you wouldn't have to worry about locking yourself out of them\u2014if you already had Auspex 4, it would be <i>easier</i> to pick up an Auspex 1 Celerity 1 Amalgam (Quicken Sight from old editions, maybe?), not harder.<br /> <br /> If the opportunity cost is removed, I like Amalgams much more than &quot;combination disciplines&quot;, which always felt like they never quite fit into the system.<br /> <br /> (Sorry for the multiple pings, the editor breaks completely if I try to quote multiple posts in a single reply, so this seems to be the only way to keep things straight.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T10:13:14-07:00","id":1401933,"title":"","content":"A thing you're forgetting with Auspex is that those powers are really weak when you only have one level of auspex. One dice premonitions usually fail, your ability to sense the unseen will usually fail, heightened senses, at -1 difficulty, aren't that significant. The only big little jump of auspex 1 is that it cuts darkness penalties in half if you don't have Eyes of the Beast.<br /> <br /> And for Disciplines, most level 1 powers were the most used, most broadly applicable powers of the discipline; Command is easier to fire off than a full mesmorize, Awe is the only subtle presence power and easily the one you'll use the most, I most often just use level 1 celerity, Eyes of the Beast might be useless if your GM doesn't pay attention to it or you don't capitalize on it, but it's fantastic when the scenario is right. Feral whispers is Godly to the point that some people don't bother getting the (actually really good) animalism powers at 3+. The first dot of fortitude is the most important dot of fortitude....<br /> <br /> With the common disciplines, the only one that has a sucker first level power is Obfuscate, which is immediately invalidated by getting the second dot (so I house rule it. No, Silence is not a good replacement, I use the effects of Arcane) First dots are awesome. They're resource cheap, they're broadly applicable, they help you hunt night-to-night<br /> <br /> Compare that to... lethal damage punches or Jumping... How does jumping high help my night-to-night hunts? (Ok, yeah, some first level powers in v5 are pretty hunt-useful, but it's clear that 'these powers are for hunters' was not a driving design feature when so many first level powers don't directly contribute to nightly unliving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T10:23:09-07:00","id":1401936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Compare that to... lethal damage punches or Jumping... How does jumping high help my night-to-night hunts </div> </div> </div>2 year later and I still not over Cat's Grace lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T04:39:03-07:00","id":1402042,"title":"","content":"You could tie extra powers/amalgams with Blood Potency (which would indirectly tie in with Generation). An extra ability at every even level (2,4,6,8,10) of Blood Potency with a limit of half your BP as power level.<br /> <br /> So, an Ancillae with BP 4 could develop two extra abilities per Discipline, with a level limit of 2. A Methuselah with BP 10 could develop up to five extra per Discipline, with level limit of 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T09:37:09-07:00","id":1402084,"title":"","content":"I was reading the intervention of Matthew Dawkins in the Justin Achili thread about amalgams and I feel there's something we missed.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disciplines will not be going above five dots. There's no need for it. It's just as easy to make amalgams.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the implication being amalgams doesn't count towards the number of powers one can have in a discipline?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T10:00:33-07:00","id":1402086,"title":"","content":"The Core book doesn't say anything like that. <br /> someone correct me<br /> Please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T10:17:22-07:00","id":1402089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402086#post1402086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Core book doesn't say anything like that.<br /> someone correct me<br /> Please?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The core book doesn't state that Amalgams are separate, and the example of buying an Amagam is in reference to buying a Discipline ass a normal slot.<br /> This was also confirmed by Karim when people were asking if you could buy an Amalgam in either Discipline (because of the 'traits of either' mention), to which he said no, if it's listed as a level in a Discipline, it is only bought in that Discipline.<br /> <br /> So I think there's probably some miscommunication regarding the use of Amalgams in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 07-10-2020, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T11:28:27-07:00","id":1402094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402086#post1402086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Core book doesn't say anything like that.<br /> someone correct me<br /> Please?</div> </div> </div> </div>RAW, amalgams take up one &quot;slot&quot; in one of their two disciplines (but not both\u2014that was an error in the first printing iirc).<br /> <br /> Houseruling that they <i>don't</i> take up slots would be an interesting way to expand their utility; that's how they were in V20 and earlier. The question then is, what should their experience cost be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T15:25:55-07:00","id":1402129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402094#post1402094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RAW, amalgams take up one &quot;slot&quot; in one of their two disciplines (but not both\u2014that was an error in the first printing iirc).<br /> <br /> Houseruling that they <i>don't</i> take up slots would be an interesting way to expand their utility; that's how they were in V20 and earlier. The question then is, what should their experience cost be?</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems arbitrary for that to apply to amalgams, but not single discipline powers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-10T17:28:35-07:00","id":1402147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402094#post1402094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RAW, amalgams take up one &quot;slot&quot; in one of their two disciplines (but not both\u2014that was an error in the first printing iirc).<br /> <br /> Houseruling that they <i>don't</i> take up slots would be an interesting way to expand their utility; that's how they were in V20 and earlier. The question then is, what should their experience cost be?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not even one of their two. An Amalgam listed in Dominate can only be purchased in Dominate; it just needs whatever else as a prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/478887731632668683/613718439814496280/Screenshot_20190821-085404_Facebook.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/478887731632668683/613718439814496280/Screenshot_20190821-085404_Facebook.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/478887731632668683/613718439814496280/Screenshot_20190821-085404_Facebook.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"> https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/478887731632668683/613718439814496280/Screenshot_20190821-085404_Facebook.jpg </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402129#post1402129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It seems arbitrary for that to apply to amalgams, but not single discipline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which part? The 'in either Discipline' (which isn't the case, per book wording and Word of God in the link) or Amalgams exist outside everything? The first one has precedent in prior editions, but isn't the case currently. IT would also change the baselines and remove powers from the various tracks, making some tracks have more powers by default than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T06:32:13-07:00","id":1402231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402147#post1402147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which part? The 'in either Discipline' (which isn't the case, per book wording and Word of God in the link) or Amalgams exist outside everything? The first one has precedent in prior editions, but isn't the case currently. IT would also change the baselines and remove powers from the various tracks, making some tracks have more powers by default than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>The suggested house rule about amalgams not taking a discipline slot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T07:04:44-07:00","id":1402237,"title":"","content":"Where is that suggested? You say it's a <i>house rule?</i> <br /> <br /> I think the move towards amalgams is a mistake and the old system of elder disciplines was much better and, respectfully; one shouldn't be writing a book according to a misinterpretation of a previous book. Perhaps if you revised V5 so that the 5-dot limit wasn't a thing, Mr Dawkins would be very right in asserting that amalgams would present us with impressive elder powers beyond what a neonate could obtain and that 6th level powers may not be necessary (even if getting previously unreachable high level abilities was for me the main appeal for diablerie; I suppose blood potency granting bonus dice can mitigate that loss to a small degree but then.... another rabbit hole) <br /> <br /> But as things are, Disciplines are one of the bigger things that keeps me with V20. Amalgams, as they are, are just more-painful-to-get discipline powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T07:15:33-07:00","id":1402238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402231#post1402231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The suggested house rule about amalgams not taking a discipline slot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The arbitrary rule has precedent from prior editions, where Combo Disciplines/Techniques were a new power built with two Discipline prereqs outside of the normal 5 power limit Discipline list.<br /> <br /> I personally think Amalgams are fine as they are, a power that requires facility in something else to use, because of the implicit combined effect.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402237#post1402237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that suggested? You say it's a <i>house rule?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's not suggested by the book. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24808_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24808\" data-vbnamecard=\"24808\">Draconis</a> suggested it as a house rule to mimic how Combo Powers used to work, not that it's implied anywhere in the book at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the move towards amalgams is a mistake and the old system of elder disciplines was much better and, respectfully; one shouldn't be writing a book according to a misinterpretation of a previous book. Perhaps if you revised V5 so that the 5-dot limit wasn't a thing, Mr Dawkins would be very right in asserting that amalgams would present us with impressive elder powers beyond what a neonate could obtain and that 6th level powers may not be necessary (even if getting previously unreachable high level abilities was for me the main appeal for diablerie; I suppose blood potency granting bonus dice can mitigate that loss to a small degree but then.... another rabbit hole)<br /> <br /> But as things are, Disciplines are one of the bigger things that keeps me with V20. Amalgams, as they are, are just more-painful-to-get discipline powers. </div> </div> </div>Amalgams are built primarily as ways to semi-gatelock powers that are typically used by certain clans, mainly, based on the design philosophy. Then you get into the concept of a Discipline power that is built using aspects of another, thematically and narratively, for how Amalgams are designed. You do realize people can mistype/misspeak without 'writing a book according to a misinterpretation'..Amalgams are specifically designed the way they are (which Dawkins had nothing to do, Karim Muammar and Kenneth Hite did the design of the mechanics), without any reference to elder stuff, regardless of misspeaking on current writers' parts. Elder stuff is now level 4/5 powers because the scale is different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 07-11-2020, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T07:27:02-07:00","id":1402240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402237#post1402237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is that suggested? You say it's a <i>house rule?</i> <br /> <br /> I think the move towards amalgams is a mistake and the old system of elder disciplines was much better and, respectfully; one shouldn't be writing a book according to a misinterpretation of a previous book. Perhaps if you revised V5 so that the 5-dot limit wasn't a thing, Mr Dawkins would be very right in asserting that amalgams would present us with impressive elder powers beyond what a neonate could obtain and that 6th level powers may not be necessary (even if getting previously unreachable high level abilities was for me the main appeal for diablerie; I suppose blood potency granting bonus dice can mitigate that loss to a small degree but then.... another rabbit hole) <br /> <br /> But as things are, Disciplines are one of the bigger things that keeps me with V20. Amalgams, as they are, are just more-painful-to-get discipline powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think disciplines are my main gripe with v5, too... Only a few 6+ powers from vtm are possible in v5, so things like became kupala and became a dragon, vozhd etc are just impossible even if you consider amalgams. Gonna stay in Revised too but if Player Guild (xtimas 2019) fix that I would be happy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T07:38:07-07:00","id":1402247,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*writes constructive argument*</span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402238#post1402238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;Do you literally have nothing constructive to say, ever?&quot; </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>If you ever feel like you need to argue in bad faith, maybe you shouldn't make the argument. It doesn't matter that MD didn't write the system initially, he made a comment about what to do with it that didn't line up with what we have; Amalgam disciplines are not-great , and I'm not &quot;edition warring&quot; with that post; I'm saying I don't like V5 doing<i> this</i> but it would be better if V5 did <i>that</i> (also, Combo disciplines sucked) . If V5 made some minor but important changes (IE dropping the 5 power limit) it'd work better for elders (Note: This looks like a pretty constructive suggestion here) and amalgams would get more time to shine (Because I would pass most of them up, the linear disciplines are more important most of the time as things are currently)<br /> <br /> I don't really get why you need to respond to a fair and balanced set of opinions with such vitriol?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-11T09:44:40-07:00","id":1402264,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Guys!<br /> <br /> Remember, mutual respect.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T07:11:14-07:00","id":1402406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402247#post1402247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">*writes constructive argument*</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> If you ever feel like you need to argue in bad faith, maybe you shouldn't make the argument. It doesn't matter that MD didn't write the system initially, he made a comment about what to do with it that didn't line up with what we have; Amalgam disciplines are not-great , and I'm not &quot;edition warring&quot; with that post; I'm saying I don't like V5 doing<i> this</i> but it would be better if V5 did <i>that</i> (also, Combo disciplines sucked) . If V5 made some minor but important changes (IE dropping the 5 power limit) it'd work better for elders (Note: This looks like a pretty constructive suggestion here) and amalgams would get more time to shine (Because I would pass most of them up, the linear disciplines are more important most of the time as things are currently)<br /> <br /> I don't really get why you need to respond to a fair and balanced set of opinions with such vitriol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Notice how I had rewritten the last part of my post (about ten minutes) before you posted this, because I thought about what I said and realized that what I said wasn't constructive to the conversation. <br /> <br /> Not sure why you're thinking my statement is in bad faith though; as I'm just stating that people misspeak. Given the circumstances of the book and RAW, that's about all we can go by. But it'd be great to have Dawkins weigh in and clarify on what he meant there. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-12T07:51:42-07:00","id":1402409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1402406#post1402406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Notice how I had rewritten the last part of my post (about ten minutes) before you posted this, because I thought about what I said and realized that what I said wasn't constructive to the conversation.<br /> <br /> Not sure why you're thinking my statement is in bad faith though; as I'm just stating that people misspeak. Given the circumstances of the book and RAW, that's about all we can go by. But it'd be great to have Dawkins weigh in and clarify on what he meant there.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://media2.giphy.com/media/7JsEgDMrziuJd9fFY1/200.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I don't instantaneously write my posts, nor do I have a live feed of your edits. Also I'm more upset about you being <i>objectively </i><i>wrong</i> with the insistence of righteousness than rude. Like if you just called me a prick... Well the mods would mind, but I wouldn't care enough to report.<br /> <br /> I've tried to reach out to MD concerning this, no avail. But I suppose that's understandable.<br /> The system as current has nothing in place for &quot;elder powers&quot;, other than the golden rule. Which is a shame because I really like VTM for it's -I as a Vampire can obtain the power to do anything another vampire can do... eventually- (Though v5 does grant stronger blood a lot of disadvantages, and you can't get all the powers in a discipline, which seem to run counter to that philosophy) That philosophy set it far apart from your average DnD game and yet encouraging Golden-rule powers tends to create NPC exclusives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T12:16:35-07:00","id":1407348,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of the old 6+ dots disciplines. Sure, they sound cool and all, but in the end, it's just fluff powers that PCs would rarely if ever have access to. The V5 method of leaving it at 5 dots, but making high BP vampires so much better at using them sounds totally fair. Although I'd perhaps add one house rule: If a vampire ever gets to 5 dots in a discipline, they can keep just keep paying for more 5 dot disciples to unlock all the other powers that the discipline offers instead of just capping at 5 powers per discipline.<br /> <br /> Also note that the reason for giving elder vampires in old editions of VTM was because, back then, disciplines didn't use their discipline dots in the roll. So nothing really marked a vampire with high discipline dots as particularly powerful at discipline usage other than simply creating new powers that were godlike in scope. Which was fundamentally broken.<br /> <br /> Now, in V5, A blood potency 7 elder with five dots in a discipline would have a *crushing* advantage against a younger weaker vamp, even if using the same powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2462-karlb","name":"KarlB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T12:23:11-07:00","id":1407351,"title":"","content":"I think that 6+ dot disciplines are just an additional dot and not nearly as impressive as people make them out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:21:13-07:00","id":1407372,"title":"","content":"The 6+ Disciplines were a poorly edited mish-mash of things that ranged from, &quot;why am I paying this much for this, it's barely as good as the 3rd dot power, can't it just be a combo Discipline so I can actually pay a reasonable price for it&quot; to, &quot;using this in the game is like whipping out a nuke.&quot; There was a distinct lack of consistency to their effects in terms of power level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T14:31:41-07:00","id":1407376,"title":"","content":"I won't make a case for levels 8 and 9, but level 6 and 7 Disciplines were realistic, achievable goals for players and likely powers for elders in your city. raising your limits from 5 to 6 or even 7 was half the reason to want to diablerise. Blood potency comes with a load of cons and doesn't hold that same appeal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T16:48:31-07:00","id":1407398,"title":"","content":"Next, rezz the &quot;Helena/Portia candid camera or real?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-14T14:31:45-07:00","id":1408240,"title":"","content":"Honestly I still think the growth should be horizontal, not vertical. Rather than adding more dots, you can simply give Elders (and Methuselah's) the ability to develop multiple powers at each given level (and more amalgams as well) and generally learn to be more diverse and adaptable with their disciplines than younger vampires (who might develop their disciplines along only one or two lines.)<br /> <br /> It's also likely that Older/more powerful vampires would not only be able to amass more abilities within a given discipline, they probably could employ them in greater numbers (and combinations) simultaneously (in a sense 'stacking' powers in a given turn because of their older, more potent blood. Sort of like how in the old game and requiem older vampires not only had more blood, but they could spend more blood per turn.)<br /> <br /> I mean Vampire powers getting closer to Caine were supposed to - in a sense - be more mutable like that the way thaumaturgy (Heck, Blood Magic made that connection ages ago - Caine's ability to create disciplines on demand was VERY similar to thaumaturgy. The difference being Caine probably didn't have to spend blood the way a Thaumaturge did. So one presumes a Elder/Methuselah 'inceptor' would also get the benefits of thaumaturgy without 'spending' blood to power it, although they should require more time to develop the new abiliteis.)<br /> <br /> You can still leave 6+ disciplines as some 'Storyteller defined' territory too. The vampiric equivalent of Archmastery from 'Horizon' and its take on '6th level' powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 08-14-2020, 05:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T05:11:51-07:00","id":1408337,"title":"","content":"I like 6+ Disciplines. I just didn't like the way White Wolf implemented them.<br /> <br /> 6+ Disciplines have their place in the setting, I think. Michael uses Presence 9 to enthrall an entire city and drive its Cainites to religious delusion. Yorak uses Vicissitude 9 to craft the Cathedral of Flesh. Strictly speaking, are they narratively necessary? Probably not, you can handwave the Cathedral's creation (&quot;amalgams&quot;) and attribute Constantinople's problems to mundane reasons rather than an insane methuselah (also) misusing his powers. 6+ Disciplines are mostly just plain <i>cool</i>. Masquerade is a game with high power levels. If you want a game with more down to earth elders, that's Requiem.<br /> <br /> White Wolf did two main things wrong with elder Disciplines, though. The first was that authors spilled way too much ink on those powers when they are largely inaccessible to PCs. They're like epic levels in D&amp;D. Only a very small subset of your customer base is going to make use of these rules on the player rather than the GM side, so it was dumb to insert random lists of 6+ powers into books like <i>Guide to the Camarilla</i>. I think the only place that 6+ Disciplines have their place is in the writeups for specific NPCs in the By Night books. Early city books had that. &quot;Gustav Breidenstein's extra Presence dots allow him to do X, Y, and Z.&quot;<br /> <br /> The other problem was that a lot of 6+ powers were stupid as 6+ powers and would've worked better as 1-5 amalgams. &quot;I turn into a tree&quot; does not need to be a 6+ power. But the system only allowed multiple powers per level at 6+ dots if amalgams weren't used, so the authors were working within the limits of the system they had. (V5 allowing players to pick between multiple powers at a given Discipline level was one of the new system's better ideas.) My personal rule for 6+ powers is that they should either work on a massive scale (Michael's city-wide &quot;still works in torpor&quot; Presence 9) or break the established rules of the Discipline/being a vampire in a way that GMs want to keep out of PC hands (Protean 9's/Serpentis 9's &quot;you can walk in the sun for a day&quot; power). Anything else probably works just fine at levels 1-5.<br /> <br /> I'm not a fan of the Requiem method of Blood Potency requirements for amalgam Disciplines, though. If you're making a 5-dot Discipline also exclusive to Blood Potency 9, that's functionally the same as making it a 9-dot Discipline. Just call a spade a spade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":3110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","user":"False Epiphany","date":". 08-15-2020, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T06:34:35-07:00","id":1408344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408337#post1408337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf did two main things wrong with elder Disciplines, though. The first was that authors spilled way too much ink on those powers when they are largely inaccessible to PCs. They're like epic levels in D&amp;D. Only a very small subset of your customer base is going to make use of these rules on the player rather than the GM side, so it was dumb to insert random lists of 6+ powers into books like <i>Guide to the Camarilla</i>. I think the only place that 6+ Disciplines have their place is in the writeups for specific NPCs in the By Night books. Early city books had that. &quot;Gustav Breidenstein's extra Presence dots allow him to do X, Y, and Z.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with most of what you said, save this part. In my experience, players will want to play with the 6+ disciplines at some point. It could be at the end of a long running campaign or just a one-off, but elders games do happen and they aren't rare edge cases.<br /> <br /> The dark ages setting even let players get 7th gen when they bought the generation background up to 5, so I think it's more a case of writers giving options to keep games fresh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T03:54:15-07:00","id":1408472,"title":"","content":"I tend to think that elders want to play like me. <br /> <br /> You're embraced as good-at-something<br /> You acquire some bare minimum skills <br /> You raise your clan disciplines, at least the ones you use, to about three or maybe four; you really try to nail that thing you're good at. <br /> You try to acquire common out of clan disciplines and skills in areas that would be considred a weakness, so that when they fuck up their primary strategy they're not completely hopeless. A malkavian likely learns potence, a Nosferatu might learn dominate, A Tremere would be wise to learn Fortitude, a Toreador is a vapid, uselesss thing that's content with their disgusting generalist disciplines, A lot of people gravitate towards either Auspex or Obfuscate. <br /> Once you have about two dots in these new disciplines, you build up your in-clans again and then you once again move to diversify again and perhaps gain third dots in your OoC's. <br /> <br /> The thing is, with out of clans, in most cases getting more than 3 dots becomes an expense that's not worth taking. In some disciplines, namely auspex, It's totally worth it, but in general disciplines in V1-V20 had broadly applicable powers at the lower levels and highly specific powers you rarely use at higher levels. In most cases I could do more with a 6th level of -that power I use all the time- than I could use with -that power I keep in reserve-. Like, If I'm a Malkavian elder, having Potence 3 is going to be pretty handy in athletics rolls and the rare, rare instances where I've been suckered into a brawl, but getting potence 4; from a cost benefit analysis, isn't really worth it. It'd be better and cheaper for me to have obfuscate 6, or raise other out of clans to 3, or perhaps even invest in a rare discipline. <br /> <br /> Now, If we were stuck in the world of V5 and my malkavian elder couldn't buy obfuscate 6, I already have impressive mundane skills, and there's nothing to buy, I suppose I could get potence 4... Mind you the powers in V5 are really specific so there's goals to work forward to and such but.... <br /> <br /> If all the elders are forced to go wide because they can't go up, wouldn't they all start to look the same?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T06:42:32-07:00","id":1408488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408472#post1408472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to think that elders want to play like me.<br /> <br /> You're embraced as good-at-something<br /> You acquire some bare minimum skills<br /> You raise your clan disciplines, at least the ones you use, to about three or maybe four; you really try to nail that thing you're good at.<br /> You try to acquire common out of clan disciplines and skills in areas that would be considred a weakness, so that when they fuck up their primary strategy they're not completely hopeless. A malkavian likely learns potence, a Nosferatu might learn dominate, A Tremere would be wise to learn Fortitude, a Toreador is a vapid, uselesss thing that's content with their disgusting generalist disciplines, A lot of people gravitate towards either Auspex or Obfuscate.<br /> Once you have about two dots in these new disciplines, you build up your in-clans again and then you once again move to diversify again and perhaps gain third dots in your OoC's.<br /> <br /> The thing is, with out of clans, in most cases getting more than 3 dots becomes an expense that's not worth taking. In some disciplines, namely auspex, It's totally worth it, but in general disciplines in V1-V20 had broadly applicable powers at the lower levels and highly specific powers you rarely use at higher levels. In most cases I could do more with a 6th level of -that power I use all the time- than I could use with -that power I keep in reserve-. Like, If I'm a Malkavian elder, having Potence 3 is going to be pretty handy in athletics rolls and the rare, rare instances where I've been suckered into a brawl, but getting potence 4; from a cost benefit analysis, isn't really worth it. It'd be better and cheaper for me to have obfuscate 6, or raise other out of clans to 3, or perhaps even invest in a rare discipline.<br /> <br /> Now, If we were stuck in the world of V5 and my malkavian elder couldn't buy obfuscate 6, I already have impressive mundane skills, and there's nothing to buy, I suppose I could get potence 4... Mind you the powers in V5 are really specific so there's goals to work forward to and such but....<br /> <br /> If all the elders are forced to go wide because they can't go up, wouldn't they all start to look the same?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They'd only be samey if you take the core book as a vacuum, but we know that's not the case, as more powers have been released in most of the books that have come out, which is in-world indicating a huge breadth of possible abilities of the blood. So elders would just have more time to research and cultivate conditions for uncommon abilities of the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T08:49:48-07:00","id":1408498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408488#post1408488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They'd only be samey if you take the core book as a vacuum, but we know that's not the case, as more powers have been released in most of the books that have come out, which is in-world indicating a huge breadth of possible abilities of the blood. So elders would just have more time to research and cultivate conditions for uncommon abilities of the blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but V5's disciplines tend toward being less flexible,even less powerful with the extra blood potency dice included(potence), and all vampires are capped at 5 powers per discipline.<br /> <br /> Elder would have to have a frankly absurd number of disciplines to make up that difference, to the point of needing 3-5 in Every common discipline, and even then could still be offed by a neonate that gets lucky.<br /> <br /> It's more a problem of scale than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T09:32:40-07:00","id":1408504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408498#post1408498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe, but V5's disciplines tend toward being less flexible,even less powerful with the extra blood potency dice included(potence), and all vampires are capped at 5 powers per discipline.<br /> <br /> Elder would have to have a frankly absurd number of disciplines to make up that difference, to the point of needing 3-5 in Every common discipline, and even then could still be offed by a neonate that gets lucky.<br /> <br /> It's more a problem of scale than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The scale is entirely different in V5 than prior editions though, across the board. So it's not really a problem; the problem is continuing a 1-to-1 comparison when the mechanic scale is KNOWN to be different. When a neonate caps out at 10-11 dice without mods with their BP, while a BP8 elder caps out at 14, there's already a scale difference. Add on surge, that neonate has an 11-12, that elder has an 18. Then stack on any other bonuses that might add to it. A neonate heals 1 damage versus a methuselah healing 4-5. A neonate adds 1 to any dice roll while a methuselah adds 4-5. You can math all this out and on averages, the methuselah is going to win. Especially a methuselah played smartly, like they should and the fiction says they do for the Jyhad, not a 'lol come at me bro!' methuselah RPG Boss Monster.<br /> <br /> And I mean, HElena's stat block has mostly 5s and a couple of 3s. And 'having 3-5 in every common Discipline' was the hallmark of old NPC sheets regardless of Generation at times, not to mention scads of out of clan Disciplines. So it's not outside of what already existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T10:15:09-07:00","id":1408509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408504#post1408504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The scale is entirely different in V5 than prior editions though, across the board. So it's not really a problem; the problem is continuing a 1-to-1 comparison when the mechanic scale is KNOWN to be different. When a neonate caps out at 10-11 dice without mods with their BP, while a BP8 elder caps out at 14, there's already a scale difference. Add on surge, that neonate has an 11-12, that elder has an 18. Then stack on any other bonuses that might add to it. A neonate heals 1 damage versus a methuselah healing 4-5. A neonate adds 1 to any dice roll while a methuselah adds 4-5. You can math all this out and on averages, the methuselah is going to win. Especially a methuselah played smartly, like they should and the fiction says they do for the Jyhad, not a 'lol come at me bro!' methuselah RPG Boss Monster.<br /> <br /> And I mean, HElena's stat block has mostly 5s and a couple of 3s. And 'having 3-5 in every common Discipline' was the hallmark of old NPC sheets regardless of Generation at times, not to mention scads of out of clan Disciplines. So it's not outside of what already existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>The scale is a problem if they want to say that all the previous editions existed at all. If V5 was it's own game, then their'd be no issue. The fact that V5 is a VTM game is what makes it an issue.<br /> <br /> I'll concede a bit on the &quot;every common discipline&quot; point, VTM is a bit notorious for not following it's own character creation rules when it comes to important NPCs. On the other hand, I will point out that said elders that had points in every common discipline And 6+ abilities won't translate to V5 at all. There is no way to give them the sheer number of powerful abilities they had in previous edition, especially if you consider that it takes several power slots to re-create what was a single ability for several disciplines. This makes many things in the lore impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T20:13:56-07:00","id":1408640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408509#post1408509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The scale is a problem if they want to say that all the previous editions existed at all. If V5 was it's own game, then their'd be no issue. The fact that V5 is a VTM game is what makes it an issue.<br /> <br /> I'll concede a bit on the &quot;every common discipline&quot; point, VTM is a bit notorious for not following it's own character creation rules when it comes to important NPCs. On the other hand, I will point out that said elders that had points in every common discipline And 6+ abilities won't translate to V5 at all. There is no way to give them the sheer number of powerful abilities they had in previous edition, especially if you consider that it takes several power slots to re-create what was a single ability for several disciplines. This makes many things in the lore impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be one of the core problems with V5. It wants to have it's cake and diablerize it too. V5 may have worked out better as a Hard reboot of the setting, instead it gets weighed down by the stuff the new system doesn't have (like 6+ disciplines for example) that explained old plotlines. Instead we get an incredibly awkward soft reboot of the setting, with mechanic and lore questions most caused by the instance of continuity with the previous game settings. And I honestly think that V5 would have been better received by those who don't like it if it would have released as VTM: Re-imagined. It would also allow for the changes in setting (such as clans of death being one clan) without a ton of WTF moments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25664-gubenyochi","name":"Gubenyochi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T23:51:27-07:00","id":1408659,"title":"","content":"To some extent the argument would shift from &quot;they ruined VtM&quot; to &quot;this is just a bad knockoff&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-17-2020, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-17T01:06:24-07:00","id":1408665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gubenyochi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408640#post1408640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might be one of the core problems with V5. It wants to have it's cake and diablerize it too. V5 may have worked out better as a Hard reboot of the setting, instead it gets weighed down by the stuff the new system doesn't have (like 6+ disciplines for example) that explained old plotlines. Instead we get an incredibly awkward soft reboot of the setting, with mechanic and lore questions most caused by the instance of continuity with the previous game settings. And I honestly think that V5 would have been better received by those who don't like it if it would have released as VTM: Re-imagined. It would also allow for the changes in setting (such as clans of death being one clan) without a ton of WTF moments.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Yeah, no edition warring.<br /> <br /> This is now an official warning since you were warned yesterday.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-18T10:02:41-07:00","id":1408967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1401716-v5-amalgams-and-advanced-disciplines?p=1408659#post1408659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To some extent the argument would shift from &quot;they ruined VtM&quot; to &quot;this is just a bad knockoff&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I doubt people would be as vocal if they kept V5 and V20 in separate pools. V5 doesn't have enough supplemental material to cover in order to completely re-imagine the setting, but that'd be forgivable if it was seem more as a spin-off than a re-boot. As it stands, it makes complete sense that there's controversy over the game.<br /> <br /> On that note, making it a spin-off would have not only given them time to build suppliments, it would have been a chance to test the waters to see what sold better and received fan-feedback over the least like rules. They could have than ran with whichever rules were the most well received and Then created a &quot;5th edition&quot; based on what they learned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}